# VitalPet — Security & Privacy Rules

These rules are non-negotiable. Any code that violates them must be rewritten before committing.

## PHI boundary
Protected Health Information (PHI) must never cross the device boundary:
- No `http`, `dio`, or `http.Client` call may carry user health data, symptom answers, pet state, or check-in history as a payload
- Push notification payloads must contain only the pet's name and generic copy — never symptom data or wellness scores
- The handoff PDF is written to a temp file via the `printing` package and passed to the native share sheet. VitalPet does not observe where the user sends it. Never log share destinations.

**If you are writing a network call, ask: could this payload contain PHI? If yes, refactor.**

## Encryption
- All drift DB access goes through `lib/core/encryption/encryption_service.dart`, which derives the SQLCipher key from `flutter_secure_storage` (backed by iOS Keychain / Android Keystore)
- The key must use `IOSOptions(accessibility: KeychainAccessibility.first_unlock_this_device)` on iOS
- Never log, cache in a `SharedPreferences`, or serialize the encryption key
- The `assets/models/` directory is in `.gitignore` — model weights are not committed

## Audit logging
Every significant data event must be recorded via `AuditLogDao.append()`:
- `CHECKIN_WRITE` — on every completed or partial check-in commit
- `AMENDMENT` — when a user edits a same-day check-in
- `FILTER_TRIGGER` — when `MedicalContentFilter` blocks SLM output (store `payloadHash`, never raw text)
- `HANDOFF_EXPORT` — when the PDF is generated (store `dayRange`)
- `DATA_EXPORT` — when the user exports JSON
- `DELETE_INITIATED` — when the user triggers data deletion

**The `audit_log` table has no update or delete operations — `AuditLogDao` exposes only `append()`.**

## Medical content filter
`MedicalContentFilter.filter(String raw)` in `lib/features/slm/medical_content_filter.dart` must be applied to every string that:
- Was generated by the SLM (`flutter_gemma`)
- Will be displayed to the user

Returns `FilterResult(safe: true, text: ...)` or `FilterResult(safe: false, text: SAFE_FALLBACK_TEXT)`. On unsafe output a `FILTER_TRIGGER` audit entry is written. **Never display raw SLM output without filtering.**

## HealthKit / Health Connect
- Request read permissions only via the `health` package. Never request write types.
- Raw health data must not be persisted in the drift DB. Read it at check-in time, pass to SLM context, then discard.
- Only derived strings (e.g. `"sleep_vs_baseline: -2.1h"`) may be stored in the check-in's `answersJson`.
- Wrap all health calls in try/catch — if permissions are revoked, continue normally with health UI hidden.

## Screen security
- Register a `WidgetsBindingObserver` in `main.dart`. When `didChangeAppLifecycleState` fires `AppLifecycleState.inactive` or `paused`, overlay a blur widget before the OS captures the app-switcher snapshot.
- On Android, call `FlutterNativePlugin.addFlags(FLAG_SECURE)` in the corresponding lifecycle callback.
- Test: background the app and verify the app-switcher shows a blurred placeholder.

## Notification payloads
Notification payloads via `flutter_local_notifications` must only contain:
- The pet's name (user-chosen — not PHI)
- Generic copy ("misses you", "is waiting")
- The pet's visual state (integer 1–5)

Never include wellness scores, symptom names, check-in answers, or any health metric.

## Third-party package policy
No analytics, advertising, or crash reporting packages without explicit review:
- No Firebase Analytics / Crashlytics (unless crash-only with user opt-in and confirmed PHI exclusion)
- No Amplitude, Mixpanel, Segment
- No advertising SDKs
- Run `bash scripts/audit_deps.sh` to verify before every release build

## Data deletion flow
When the user triggers "Delete All Data":
1. Set `pet_state.deletionScheduledAt` to now — start 7-day recovery window
2. Write `DELETE_INITIATED` to audit log
3. On next app launch after 7 days: call `EncryptionService.destroyKey()` which removes the key from `flutter_secure_storage` — the drift DB is permanently unreadable without it
